WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.720
Well, we got a little baby naming drama

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.070
I want your take on.

3
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.170
The Sun reports a woman in the UK

4
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.110
posted this dilemma online.

5
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.610
She and her husband, they're about to have a little baby.

6
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.780
And they finally, after discussing it,

7
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.310
they finally picked out a name, Miles,

8
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.780
which is such a cute name.

9
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.890 line:15%
The only problem is when she told her best friend,

10
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.870 line:15%
the best friend totally gasped (gasps)

11
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.870 line:15%
because Miles is the name

12
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.140 line:15%
that she had picked out for her future son.

13
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.670 line:15%
Now, her friend is not pregnant right now though,

14
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.600 line:15%
but she plans one day she wants to have a baby.

15
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.060 line:15%
But she seemed genuinely disappointed that, you know,

16
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.590 line:15%
her friend had snatched the name.

17
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.520 line:15%
So this woman wanted to know,

18
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.650 line:15%
should she feel guilty right now

19
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.590 line:15%
for planning to name her son Miles,

20
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.830 line:15%
or should she just go like forward with it?

21
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.437 line:15%
I have a strong opinion, but I'm curious what you-

22
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:47.870 line:15%
I have some really strong opinions.

23
00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:48.703 line:15%
Ooh.

24
00:00:48.703 --> 00:00:51.190 line:15%
Audience, guests, raise your hand

25
00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.173 line:15%
if you think she should go with the name.

26
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.420
Raise your hand

27
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.550
if you think she shouldn't name her son Miles

28
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.130
because her friend likes it.

29
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.575
Nobody, okay.
Oh, all right.

30
00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:04.408
Well.
All right,

31
00:01:04.408 --> 00:01:05.930
so I think this is a one-way street here.

32
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.520
Yeah, well what about you? What do you think?

33
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.650
No!

34
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.140
She shouldn't back off.

35
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.965
She should just stick with Miles, no matter her friend says?

36
00:01:12.965 --> 00:01:15.623
Yes, you're not even pregnant!

37
00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:21.970
And how about instead of making my big moment not about you.

38
00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.790
Why couldn't they both be Miles?

39
00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.780
Do you guys remember in like elementary school?

40
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.810
I had so many Jennifers in my class.

41
00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.900
There was like Jennifer W, Jennifer D, Jennifer C.

42
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.150
I still have one of them saved as Jennifer C in my phone.

43
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.710
Like, and we all were fine. So there can be two Miles.

44
00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.050
Chill out, girl. Plus, you don't have a baby yet.

45
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.112
Right?

46
00:01:41.112 --> 00:01:41.950
(Drew sighs)

47
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.380
I know.
All right, and finally,

48
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.720
a pic from "Drew's Little Yellow Book."

49
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.490
It's a little yellow book that I curate every week

50
00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.610
for you, because I love to share.

51
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.520
And this week is very important.

52
00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.500
Today kicks off Black History Month and we are celebrating

53
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.720
with putting the spotlight on Gyrl Wonder.

54
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.540
They are a nonprofit doing incredible work

55
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.390
to support young women of color

56
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.850 line:15%
reaching for the careers of their dreams,

57
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.370 line:15%
and their extensive mentorship program

58
00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.760 line:15%
pairs young women with professionals

59
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.040
for special one-on-one tutelage and relationships.

60
00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.920
And we're donating $1,000

61
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.500
to that incredible team at Gyrl Wonder to support you

62
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.670
and thank you for all that you do.

63
00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.730 line:15%
To find out more about them and how you can get involved,

64
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.670 line:15%
please go to our website at TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com

65
00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.344 line:15%
or the little yellow book.

66
00:02:32.344 --> 00:02:35.011 line:15%
(bright music)

